  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/longContentPages/0",
    "raw": "Although the X'i race seems unwilling to divulge their history to organic historians such as us, expeditions into abandoned territory allow us to explore and estimate based on texts left behind. One large abandoned city filled to the brim with mounds of solidified graphite had an unusual journal left behind that appears to mention some sort of enormous underground monster that fed on X'i and other supposed 'entities'.\nThere was a poor sketch of it, and the only recognizable feature of the animal was a head somehow resembling a Platybelodons from Earth. According to the journal, it used thousands of strawlike tongues to drink the radioactive energy straight out of its prey.\nIt may also be the culprit behind the mounds of solidified graphite. Of course, there is always the possibility that the graphite mounds are fossilized X'i ancestors. We'll likely know, once we learn how to comprehend the structure of the X'i...and they aren't helpful in this regard.",
    "value": "尽管艾肯一族似乎不愿向我们这类有机体历史学者透露他们的过往，但通过对废弃区域的考察，我们仍能依据遗留文本进行探索与推测。一座被大量凝固石墨堆填满的废弃巨城中，留下一份不寻常的记录，其中提及某种以艾肯及其他所谓“实体”为食的巨大地下怪物。\n记录中附有一张粗糙的草图，该生物唯一可辨的特征是其头部，竟与地球上的铲齿象有几分相似。据记载，它通过数千根稻草状的舌头，直接吸取猎物体内的放射性能量。\n这些石墨堆或许正是该巨兽所为。当然，也存在另一种可能：石墨堆实为艾肯祖先的化石。若想进一步确认，恐怕需先理解艾肯自身的构造方式....而他们显然无意在此事上提供任何帮助。"
